    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not that simple though. it feels more biological than just \"trauma.\" i look at their medical records and then i look at mine, and the patterns are identical. it's like i'm watching a movie i've already seen a thousand times just waiting for the final scene. why does everyone insist on \"fighting it\" when the fight itself is just more exhaustion? it feels like i'm just fighting against physics.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
